course: dictionary
lesson: 10905
title: Visit: one word, many uses
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Visit is a good example. Most often it means to go and see a person or a place for a while.
explain: «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law, and in-laws do not always find long visits easy.» Here a visit is the time you spend with someone. The word long tells you the stay can be short or long.
explain: Visit can also be a noun, a thing you do: «A shaky voice before a hospital visit means a grown-up is scared.» Here a visit is the trip itself. Visits is the plural, for more than one visit.
explain: Sometimes visit means something else. You can visit a website, which means looking at it on a screen. Check the other words in the sentence to find the right meaning.
fact: To visit means to go to see a person or a place for a while.
fact: A visit is the time you spend there, or the trip itself.
fact: To visit a website means to look at it on a screen.
fact: A doctor or nurse who visits a sick person comes to their home to help.
fact: Useful phrases: «pay a visit», «a visit to» a place, «on a visit», and «visiting hours», when people may come to a hospital.
exercise: «Foster carers are checked and trained, and social workers visit to make sure children are safe.» What does visit mean here? | To have a long rest | To run away | To look at a screen | *To go and see people for a while to check on them
exercise: Sam says, «We are going to visit the museum on Saturday.» What does visit mean? | To paint a picture | To look at a website | To feel scared | *To go to a place and see it for a while
exercise: In «A shaky voice before a hospital visit means a grown-up is scared», what is the visit? | A website | A kind of medicine | *A trip to see someone, and the time you spend there | A sad feeling
test: «Ella will visit the website to see the new photos.» What does visit mean here? | To go to the website in a car | To shout at the website | *To look at the website on a screen | To sell the website
test: Dad says, «We will pay a visit to Aunt Amy on Sunday.» What does pay a visit mean? | *To go and see her for a while | To give her some money | To send her a letter | To stop talking to her
exam: Which sentence uses visit as a noun, meaning the trip itself? | «We visit the farm every summer.» | *«We had a lovely visit to the farm.» | «Please visit the website now.»
